  "stem": "If \\(\\frac{x}{y} = \\frac{3}{4}\\), where \\(y \\ne 0\\), what is the value of \\(\\frac{x + 2y}{y}\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "11/4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Split the fraction: \\(\\frac{x + 2y}{y} = \\frac{x}{y} + 2\\).",
    "Substitute \\(\\frac{x}{y} = \\frac{3}{4}\\): \\(\\frac{3}{4} + 2 = \\frac{11}{4}\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, y = symbols('x y')\nexpr = (x + 2*y)/y\nans = simplify(expr.subs(x, Rational(3, 4)*y))\nassert ans == Rational(11, 4)\nassert len(spr_answers) == 1 and Rational(spr_answers[0]) == ans",
